{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 8: Token Prediction",
  "description": "See how language models predict the next word!\n\nTHIS IS WHAT LLMs DO:\n1. Token -> Embedding (word becomes vector)\n2. LSTM processes context (remembers sequence)\n3. Linear projects to vocabulary size\n4. Softmax converts to probabilities\n5. Sample next token!\n\nTHE KEY INSIGHT:\nThe network learns which words follow which words.\n'The cat sat on the ___' -> probably 'mat' or 'floor'\n\nTRY THIS:\n1. Select different input tokens\n2. Watch probability distribution change\n3. See which tokens become likely\n4. Run multiple steps to generate sequences!\n\nThis is the foundation of GPT, Claude, and every LLM.",
  "metadata": {
    "created": "2025-12-19T21:30:00.000000",
    "modified": "2025-12-19T21:30:00.000000",
    "author": "Noodlings Tutorial",
